# Hide on the Ceiling: "If a double-faced card is exiled this way, it will return to the battlefield with its front face up, regardless of which face was
# up when it was exiled" (the ruling, CR 712.14). Bot1's Concealing Curtains is transformed into Revealing Eye (3/4 menace), then exiled with X = 1; at the end
# step it returns as the Concealing Curtains, a 0/4 defender, and is a new object.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Concealing Curtains
Hide on the Ceiling
Plains x3
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Concealing Curtains.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Revealing Eye.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hide on the Ceiling.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Revealing Eye)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Exile.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Concealing Curtains.Keywords = Defender
